--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `NLogN.Take`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.Runs.take {q a b d e : Fin S} (hqa : q ≠ a) (hqb : q ≠ b) (hqd : q ≠ d) (hqe : q ≠ e)
--       (hab : a ≠ b) (had : a ≠ d) (hae : a ≠ e) (hbd : b ≠ d) (hbe : b ≠ e) (hde : d ≠ e)
--       (σ : St S) (A Bw : List Bool) (ra rb : List Sym)
--       (hA : σ.stk a = A.map codeBit ++ ra) (hB : σ.stk b = Bw.map codeBit ++ rb)
--       (hra : bitOf ra.head? = none) (hrb : bitOf rb.head? = none) :
--       Runs I prog (NLogN.take q a b d e : Stmt S P) σ
--         ((((σ.set a ((A.drop Bw.length).map codeBit ++ ra)).set b rb).set d
--           (((A.take Bw.length).map codeBit).reverse ++ σ.stk d)).set e
--           ((Bw.map codeBit).reverse ++ σ.stk e)) (takeCost Bw.length)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Lockstep transfer: `take`
--
--   While the top of `b` is a bit, pop it and push it on `e`; at the same time, if the top of `a` is a
--   bit, move it to `d`.  So `|Bw|` bits are taken from `a`, where `Bw` is the bit word on `b`.
